0,25.0],[37399,25.0],[37400,10.0],[38899,10.0]],"y1":[[36400,28.0],[37399,28.0],[37400,62.0],[38899,62.0]],"y2":[[36400,62.0],[37399,62.0],[37400,24.0],[38899,24.0]]},{"label":"TLS ▸ ▚▞▚▞▚","p":1.0,"show":[[0,false],[38900,true],[40400,false]],"type":"packet","x1":25.0,"x2":10.0,"y1":62.0,"y2":24.0},{"label":"200 OK, HTML","p":1.0,"show":[[0,false],[40400,true]],"type":"packet","x1":25.0,"x2":10.0,"y1":62.0,"y2":24.0}],"header":"INTERACTIVE · ENCAPSULATION ·· ONE HEADER PER LAYER","note":[[0,"The browser writes its request, a few hundred bytes of plain text."],[1500,"TLS encrypts it with the session key. From here on, no machine along the path can read it."],[3000,"TCP adds its header: the destination port (which program on the server) and a sequence number (where these bytes sit in the stream)."],[4500,"IP adds the source and destination addresses, the only part routers along the way will read."],[6000,"The Wi-Fi frame addresses the packet one hop only, to your home router, nothing further."],[7500,"Your home router strips the frame, rewrites your private source address to your public one (NAT), and wraps the same packet in a new frame for the ISP link."],[10400,"Your ISP's router repeats the move: strip the frame, read the IP destination, wrap a new frame for the next link. Nothing inside is touched."],[13300,"The packet crosses onto a backbone network owned by someone else entirely. Same swap, no coordination needed, nothing read past the IP header."],[16200,"A last boundary into the server's network, a last new frame. The IP header and everything inside it are unchanged since your device."],[19100,"The server unwraps in reverse. The frame has served its final hop."],[20600,"The IP header carried it across the world and is done."],[22100,"TCP slotted the bytes into order and hands over a clean stream."],[23600,"And only the server, holding the session key, turns the ciphertext back into the request."],[25900,"The response \"200 OK\" and the page, is encrypted with the same session key and wrapped in the same layers for the trip back."],[27400,"It retraces the path (as dozens of packets, in reality), each hop again replacing only the outermost frame."],[38900,"Your device unwraps in the same order, frame, IP, and TCP have each done their job."],[40400,"And your browser, holding the session key, decrypts the page. Only the two endpoints ever saw plain bytes."]]}